From: NanoSoC het-chiplet testing
Subject: [PATCH] fix(d2d): arm the compute die's role lock — F7

Without SELF_ARM_TRAIN_EN the compute die has NO armed role-lock route, so
the heterogeneous link cannot reach FCSM=4 at all.

`role_locked` is a mutual clock enable, not a status bit:
    wire wlink_por_reset = ~poresetn | ~role_locked;
        (axi_chiplet_controller.sv:801, feeding .por_reset at :1575)
so with it low the Wlink is held in POR and nothing can train.

All four arming routes are closed on the built image:
    SW W1S of ROLE_CFG[1]  unreachable — ps_m omits d2d0/d2d1 (H2)
    mask_hs_bypass_i       tied 1'b0 in the FPGA wrapper (:259)
    nego_lost_w            NEGO_CFG_RESET = 7'h00, never overridden
    SELF_ARM_TRAIN_EN      1'b0, the tidelink_top default (:227)

The eth die works precisely because it sets this (nanosoc_eth_chiplet.sv:655,
its I1 fix). Link 1 gets it too: self-arm is a property of the die, not the
cable, and leaving link 1 unable to role-lock would reintroduce F7 the moment
a second ribbon is fitted.

Verify with no board: the het test repo's `make test-offline` runs
L0-BUILD-01, which is xfail(strict) today and will FAIL once this lands —
that failure is the signal to flip the gate to a plain assertion.

diff --git a/src/rtl/nanosoc_compute_chiplet.sv b/src/rtl/nanosoc_compute_chiplet.sv
--- a/src/rtl/nanosoc_compute_chiplet.sv
+++ b/src/rtl/nanosoc_compute_chiplet.sv
@@ -698 +698 @@
-    tidelink_top #(.NUM_PHY_LANES(NUM_PHY_LANES)) u_tidelink_0 (
+    tidelink_top #(.NUM_PHY_LANES(NUM_PHY_LANES), .SELF_ARM_TRAIN_EN(1'b1)) u_tidelink_0 (
@@ -899 +899 @@
-    tidelink_top #(.NUM_PHY_LANES(NUM_PHY_LANES)) u_tidelink_1 (
+    tidelink_top #(.NUM_PHY_LANES(NUM_PHY_LANES), .SELF_ARM_TRAIN_EN(1'b1)) u_tidelink_1 (
